{
  "id": "gender-coding",
  "term": "gender coding",
  "definition": "Gender coding is a pattern in a language or learning system in which words or cues are linked to male or female referents, allowing people to learn and use those links to form expectations about gender. In this context, it refers to associating features of words with the gender of the things or people they refer to, even when that pattern is learned implicitly.",
  "field": "learning",
